-- A written value that holds a call that names its inputs is not checked
-- against the other rules of the callee's name, so a site whose choice only that
-- value's type would settle stays ambiguous, as it was before TYPICALLY. The
-- rules are named by what they take, and each site is an error that says so.
-- (ok/typically-overload-nested.l4 has the ways to write the value so that it
-- is checked.)

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN base IS A STRING
      factor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS factor

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
double MEANS x TIMES 2

-- 1. The value is a call that names its input.
#EVAL scaled WITH base IS (double WITH x IS 5)

-- 2. A rule called inside a rule called, four deep: the value of each of the
-- outer sites holds a named call.
#EVAL (scaled WITH base IS (scaled WITH base IS (scaled WITH base IS (scaled WITH base IS 1))))

-- 3. A value that builds a record is a named call too.
DECLARE Order HAS total IS A NUMBER
DECLARE Refund HAS total IS A NUMBER

GIVEN order IS AN Order
      markup IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2
GIVETH A NUMBER
levy MEANS order's total TIMES markup

GIVEN order IS A Refund
      cap IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
levy MEANS order's total MINUS cap

#EVAL levy WITH order IS (Order WITH total IS 50)
